    "lawCode": "Amd §168-a, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S1036\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to designating February\nfourteenth, to be known as \"Congenital Heart Defects Awareness Day\",\nas a day of commemoration\n\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to establish a commemoration day to help\nincrease the awareness of and support the families that have suffered\na loss of a child due to a congenital heart defect.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1: Amends Executive Law section 168-a(3) to establish\nCongenital Heart Defects Awareness Day\" to increase the public\nawareness of persons who have or are at risk of having congenital\nheart defect condition.\n\n EXISTING LAW :\n\nSuch a commemoration day does not exist under current law.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe organization, \"It's My Heart\", maintains that Congenital Heart\nDefects (CHD's) is the number one serious birth defect that affects\nbabies born in the United States. It is estimated that I ill every 100\nbabies has such a condition and that number effects approximately\n40,000 children each year. Further, that twice as many children die\neach year from CHD's than from all forms of childhood cancers\ncombined. It is important to provide awareness, support and education\nto families and to the community at large about congenital heart\ndefects. Utilizing methods such as establishing a distinctive license\nplates and a special awareness day for this serious condition can help\nto increase awareness of this condition and assist families that have\nsuffered a loss due to CHD.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nS.7247 of 2008\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n LOCAL FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediate.\n",
